<section class="section reveal" id="what-is-mlops">
  <span class="section-label">Fundamentals</span>
  <h2>What Is MLOps?</h2>

  <p>Machine Learning Operations (MLOps) is a set of practices, tools, and cultural norms that bridges the gap between machine learning development and production operations. If DevOps brought discipline to software deployment, MLOps brings the same rigor to machine learning systems — ensuring that models are reproducible, testable, monitorable, and updatable at enterprise scale.</p>

  <div class="analogy">
    <h4>💡 Think of It This Way</h4>
    <p>Consider a traditional manufacturing plant versus a smart factory. A traditional plant is run by humans following procedures. A smart factory has sensors, automated quality checks, and self-adjusting machinery. MLOps is the operational framework that turns ad-hoc model development into a smart, self-monitoring system where experiments are tracked, data is versioned, models are validated automatically, and issues are detected before they impact users.</p>
  </div>

